comments[44]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-26T10:19:50.183Z",codex-agent,PR #236 links the #228 tracker item. Its merge commit 1504164 is the base of this work. Checking each reader contract on this base before changing the implementation.
  "2026-11-26T10:21:49.569Z",codex-agent,"Baseline 1504164 failed all seven new contract tests (0/7). First isolated reverts: restoring listTreeEntries accepted an unrepresentable name and failed its rejection assertion. Restoring parseBatchResponse accepted a signed size and failed its framing assertion. Restoring the fixes passed both regressions (2/2). Valid Unicode, the literal replacement character, and zero-byte objects remain supported."
  "2026-11-26T10:29:01.212Z",codex-agent,"The separate #228 tracker-link repair, PR #238, is now on origin/main at ebf9157. Fast-forwarded to it before bundle regeneration. PR #236 was the reader implementation used for the initial reproductions."
  "2026-11-26T10:35:10.152Z",codex-agent,"Isolated behavioral reverts failed for every finding. (1) lossy name decoding missed the required rejection. (3) permissive sizes, missing separator validation and ignored EOF each failed the framing corpus. (2) fetching all blobs exposed excluded objects; restoring buffered cat-file hit ENOBUFS on 66 MiB of included payloads. (4) disabling clean-byte comparison wrote the converted candidate. (5) validating modes before selection rejected an excluded gitlink. (6) write-tree on the real index changed its bytes. (7) removing either regular-file guard failed its working or committed/staged configuration check. With fixes restored, the pinned pm test command passed 91/91 on Node 26."
  "2026-11-26T10:42:06.241Z",codex-agent,Native Bun exposed stale implicit process environments for Git child processes. Passing the current environment explicitly preserved the caller-selected split index under Bun. The shared subprocess transport now reports launch failures consistently. All six affected Bun assertions passed after the correction.
  "2026-11-26T11:42:04.462Z",codex-agent,"Node 22 PR-profile group 1 ran 23 referencing files. Passed 434 of 438, 0 failed, 4 skipped. Command: PM_TEST_DEPTH=quick node --expose-gc --no-concurrent-array-buffer-sweeping --test --test-concurrency=1 test/bisect.test.ts test/derivation-provenance.test.ts test/annotate.test.ts test/release-workflow.test.ts test/duplicate-events.test.ts test/composition-consumer.test.ts test/instances.test.ts test/explicit-moves.test.ts test/ref-publication-recovery.test.ts test/layer-null-write-attribution-repair.test.ts test/tracker-lenses.test.ts test/ledger.test.ts test/control-directories.test.ts test/surface.test.ts test/dependency-refresh-workflow.test.ts test/edges.test.ts test/attribution.test.ts test/tracker-admission-review.test.ts test/verify-release-changelog-date.test.ts test/issue-26-regression.test.ts test/audit-git-identities.test.ts test/ci-routing.test.ts test/release-preparation.test.ts"
  "2026-11-26T11:42:08.118Z",codex-agent,"Node 22 PR-profile group 2 ran 21 referencing files. Passed 839 of 839, 0 failed, 0 skipped. Command: PM_TEST_DEPTH=quick node --expose-gc --no-concurrent-array-buffer-sweeping --test --test-concurrency=1 test/composition.test.ts test/resolution-propagation.test.ts test/worktree-races.test.ts test/checkpoints.test.ts test/phase6-staging.test.ts test/erasure-fragment-repairs.test.ts test/tracker-admission.test.ts test/repo.test.ts test/tracker-self-host-candidate.test.ts test/staging-snapshot-crash.test.ts test/preview.test.ts test/self-host.test.ts test/merge-move-planning.test.ts test/vcs-commands.test.ts test/tracker-capture-races.test.ts test/git.test.ts test/publication-faults.test.ts test/worktree-walk-race.test.ts test/worktree.test.ts test/c8-gaps.test.ts test/ci-codeql.test.ts"
  "2026-11-26T11:42:11.094Z",codex-agent,"Native Bun 1.3.14 passed all 93 reader and tracker-candidate tests. Additional isolated reverts failed on a Unicode release workflow inventory, a raw symlink target, and a legal control byte inside Git log subjects and filenames. Restoring the status-slot-aware parser passed its fixture. Node and Bun consumers use the same lossless Git reader before rendering JSON or TOON."
  "2026-11-26T11:48:53.822Z",codex-agent,"Targeted validation on the corrected reader: 45 Node 22 test files at PR depth, 1279 passed and 4 full-depth-only consumer cases skipped (0 failed or cancelled). The single full-depth composition consumer file then passed 6/6 with all four built/packed Node and native Bun cases exercised. The pm-linked Node 26 reader suite passed 91/91 and native Bun passed 93/93 across the reader and tracker candidate. Typecheck, build, test build, lint, duplicate and docstring checks, identity audit (5 approved identities), and real package privacy (365 files) passed. The exact-gates file contributed 6 passing tests to the PR-depth total. Reverting the structured Git-log marker handling also failed its legal control-byte subject/path regression; the corrected case passed. The branch CI runs are recorded at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/workflows/ci.yml?query=branch%3Afix%2Fself-host-reader-post-merge-review ."
  "2026-11-26T11:56:53.580Z",codex-agent,"Checking a review finding on the first PR head: Git may transcode commit metadata to the configured log output encoding while leaving valid path bytes raw. The regression will exercise real history reads under this setting alongside unrepresentable path rejection."
  "2026-11-26T11:58:02.504Z",codex-agent,"Confirmed review thread PRRT_kwDOToJT7M68XgAe on the first PR head: the real repository fixture with i18n.logOutputEncoding=ISO-8859-1 and a Unicode subject failed with invalid_git_path (0/1). Requesting UTF-8 metadata for the Git log operation made the same regression pass (1/1), including the unchanged assertions for raw invalid filename rejection and valid control bytes in subject and path. The only behavior change between those runs was the Git log encoding option."
  "2026-11-26T12:00:39.649Z",codex-agent,"Review correction validation passed: Node 22 git, ledger, reader and tracker-candidate suites 114/114; Node 26 pm-linked reader 91/91 plus isolated encoding regression 1/1; native Bun reader and tracker-candidate suites 93/93. Typecheck, build, test build, lint, zero-duplication gate, docstring gate (622 declarations), pack privacy (365 files, zero findings) and identity audit (5 approved) passed again. PR checks: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/pull/240/checks . The first-head release gate, Windows launchers and CodeQL passed before this correction. First-head run: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/45814229698 ."
  "2026-11-26T12:12:34.062Z",codex-agent,"The dynamic test environment audit in CI found the two Git child launches in the Unicode workflow fixture inherited the ambient process environment. The local fixture passed, but the suite-wide source audit failed on that exact fixture. CI job: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/45815930752/job/139895860188 ."
  "2026-11-26T12:14:29.198Z",codex-agent,"The Unicode release-source fixture now launches both Git children with the shared synthetic testEnvironment(). The original CI run failed its dynamic entrypoint/source audit with implicit ambient environment. After the correction, Node 26 passed all 31 tests in test/test-environment.test.ts and test/verify-release-changelog-date.test.ts, including the same repository-wide audit. Typecheck, test build, lint, docstrings, duplicates, package privacy and identities passed again. No production behavior changed in this correction."
  "2026-11-26T12:16:03.976Z",codex-agent,"The two fixture/audit files also passed 31/31 on Node 22. The shared-runner hold is checked before each push. Exact-head checks and their run links are available at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/pull/240/checks ."
  "2026-11-26T13:03:40.950Z","harness:pi",Continuing the PR 240 follow-up on this branch. The auto re-review left three non-blocking findings on the reader (inherited Git pathspec settings breaking the --literal-pathspecs lookup; the regular-file classification in the working reader re-reading the path after the bytes were captured; the staged writer's scratch index copy dropping a split index's sharedindex base). Verified each finding against the current branch and reproduced the first (Git dies with 'global literal pathspec setting is incompatible' under GIT_GLOB_PATHSPECS/GIT_ICASE_PATHSPECS) and the third (git write-tree fails with 'index file open failed' when the shared base sits only beside the selected index) with scratch repositories; closing each class across the package now.
  "2026-11-26T14:23:17.383Z",pi-glm,"Re-review round 2: all three non-blocking findings verified valid and fixed, class-wide. (1) Pathspec isolation (self-host tree lookup): git dies with 'global literal pathspec setting is incompatible with all other global pathspec settings' when a --literal-pathspecs child inherits GIT_GLOB_PATHSPECS or GIT_ICASE_PATHSPECS (verified on git 2.53). Rule: a git child whose pathspec semantics the tool pins must not inherit ambient GIT_*_PATHSPECS settings. New isolatedPathspecEnvironment() in git.ts strips the four variables for every runGit child and for the reader's ls-tree spawn; the class instances beyond the finding site are the preflight tracker-cleanliness status (now also pinned with --literal-pathspecs so a tracker path with metacharacters cannot glob-sweep siblings) and the release-changelog-date source inventory, which relies on git's default matching and silently lost every workflow under an ambient GIT_LITERAL_PATHSPECS. (2) Tied classification (working reader): the rule is that a decision about captured bytes never comes from a second observation of the same path. readSourceFiles now classifies by the leaf type the engine observed when it read (readWorkingFile exposes the pre-read symbolicLink) and refuses any path whose identity changed mid-read; the same split existed in loadConfig (type verdict from one lstat, bytes from a second open) and in writeSnapshot's unchanged check (type from one lstat, bytes from a separate read), both now identity-guarded with the engine's sameFileIdentity; the bundle write itself lands through a same-directory temp + rename so a swapped-in link at the bundle path is replaced, not followed. Engine destruction paths were checked and are already stat-pinned at the action (durability retire/claim refuse destructive_target_changed), so no further instances of the rule are unguarded in the package. (3) Shared index base (staged writer): reproduced that git resolves a split index's base beside the index first with git-dir fallback, and write-tree on a copy without the base fails exactly with 'index file open failed' when the base sits only beside the caller's index; the scratch copy now carries every sharedindex.* sibling, tolerating one garbage-collected between listing and copy."
  "2026-11-26T14:23:27.484Z",pi-glm,"Revert proofs (behavioral revert of each fix in a disposable copy of the sources, tests rerun, fixed sources restored byte-identical and rerun green). Class A: reverting the pathspec isolation and the literal pin made all three regressions fail — the self-host tree-lookup test died with 'git ls-tree failed: fatal: global literal pathspec setting is incompatible with all other global pathspec settings', the preflight tracker-cleanliness test reported the sibling's uncommitted edit as tracker dirt (warn instead of pass), and the release inventory test lost the workflow file entirely; restored, 3/3 pass. Class B: reverting the tied classification and identity guards made all three mid-read replacement regressions fail — the working writer returned the captured CRLF bytes unverified instead of refusing, the configuration loader parsed the captured bytes instead of refusing, and the unchanged check skipped the rewrite leaving a symbolic link at the bundle path; restored, 3/3 pass. Class C: reverting the sharedindex sibling copy failed the staged-writer regression with the finding's exact error, 'fatal: <scratch>/sharedindex.<oid>: index file open failed: No such file or directory'; restored, 1/1 pass."
  "2026-11-26T14:33:39.534Z",pi-glm,"Round-2 gates on the branch: reader and tracker-candidate suites 96/96 and 32/32, preflight 20/20, changelog-date 26/26, the seven new class regressions 7/7 under their linked command, and the full referencing sweep of 37 files plus the test-environment source audit passed 1309 cases with 0 failures at 2 workers (quick depth). Typecheck, build, lint (zero warnings), duplication gate 0%, docstring gate 631 declarations, git identity audit (5 approved addresses), and pack privacy (365 files, 0 findings) all pass; changelog:check reports up to date and the regenerated bundle passes accept:self-host at the round-2 head. The round-2 fix commit is e24948e. Exact-head checks and run links for this push are at the pull request's checks page: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/pull/240/checks . Stopping here per the continuation instruction; the orchestrator verifies the auto-review round."
  "2026-11-26T14:33:57.867Z",pi-glm,"Correction to the previous comment's totals: the sweep ran 39 test files — all 37 files that import the touched modules, plus the dynamic test-environment source audit and the identity-audit suite — with 1275 cases passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (474 + 584 + 75 + 96 + 20 + 26)."
  "2026-11-26T14:52:20.684Z",pi-glm,"CI caught one violation the local sweep missed (its audit suite imports no touched module): the durability source audit rejects the raw fs rename/remove calls the unchanged-bundle rewrite first used. The bundle write now publishes through the engine's own durability boundary (durability.rename for the same-directory rename over the target, durability.discardTemporary for the failed-write cleanup), matching the policy every other production rename in the package follows. The audit test passes locally, and the mid-read replacement regression still passes with the policy-compliant write."
  "2026-11-26T15:25:39.381Z",pi-glm,"Exact-head CI at 25a0843 (run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/45844964105 ): 21 jobs green — every quick shard including the durability audit shard that failed at the previous head, the release gate (typecheck, build, lint, duplicates, docstrings, all acceptance fixtures, identity audit, pack privacy, changelog check, both release verifiers, tracked pm health), both Windows acceptance launchers, and all eight coverage shards. coverage-merge failed while downloading the shard artifacts with 'digest-mismatch: error' from the artifact digest verification, and the test (26) summary job failed only downstream of it; no test or gate failed at this head. The earlier head 0605ab5 (run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/45840663505 ) failed its durability source audit on the raw fs rename the bundle rewrite first used, fixed by publishing through durability.rename in 25a0843. Recording this round's outcome as the last tracker write; the round-2 head with the evidence committed is next."
  "2026-11-26T16:02:42.778Z",pi-glm,"The 3694b46 coverage merge exposed a real gap my local sweep could not see (the c8 threshold only runs in CI's merge step): the sharedindex sibling copy's ENOENT-tolerant catch and its non-file filter had no covering tests, leaving the reader file under the 100% per-file threshold. Two adversarial tests close it: one makes a stale base vanish between the directory listing and its copy (the copy must skip it and still write) and plants a directory with the shared-base prefix (skipped unread), the other fails the copy with EACCES and requires the write to fail loudly rather than silently dropping a base. Focused c8 now reports the reader file at 100% lines with the only uncovered branch being the module's pre-existing main-invocation guard, which the full suite covers as before; the shared-base and sibling regressions all pass (10/10 under the updated linked command)."
  "2026-11-26T16:39:34.513Z",codex-agent,"Continued PR #240 at 2aea4fb. The branch already includes the issue 228 fix and matches the remote. The review targets four shared rules: bind file type and reads to one descriptor, feed the actual captured bytes to conversion, reuse one configuration observation, and read only the dependency named by the frozen index. The stale-base reproducer will assert that unrelated paths are never read."
  "2026-11-26T16:53:48.103Z",codex-agent,"The focused regressions passed 14/14. The staged writer uses Git's primary shared-index location first, then the selected index's directory. A private Git directory and the original common object store keep the caller's base mtime and index bytes intact. The stale-base test now triggers removal at the stale file's own copy or open boundary and requires zero such attempts. Tests also cover a genuinely required unreadable, missing, non-regular or symlinked base."
  "2026-11-26T17:06:09.512Z",codex-agent,"Package-wide descriptor audit found the same pattern in native buffered and streaming worktree capture, layer checks, Git-tracked release source reads, refs, collection roots, control JSON, pack recovery, bisect owners, and erasure/destruction records. The same file-type validation and nonblocking read flags now cover those paths. SDK and CLI use the same repository methods before JSON or TOON rendering. Existing fault assertions now track the chosen descriptor, preserving their original injected failures. Node 26 passed all 15 focused cases."
  "2026-11-26T17:12:44.432Z",codex-agent,"Isolated behavioral reverts failed 11 assertions across seven changes. A pathname read accepted or consumed replacement bytes in both configuration and bundle tests. Pathname-based clean hashing failed after the late replacement. Rereading configuration made four observations and selected with different exclusions than the archived configuration. The old sibling loop attempted a stale read, rejected an unsplit index beside an EACCES sibling, and lost a required symlinked base. Removing the inode check failed both working-source and native staging capture. Restoring raw metadata and release-source reads exposed the corresponding nonregular replacements. Fixed Node 22 and Node 26 focused runs passed, and Bun 1.3.14 passed all 109 self-host and tracker-candidate tests."
  "2026-11-26T17:56:45.634Z",codex-agent,"The two native metadata fallback reverts each misclassified a captured JSON null as absence after a concurrent removal. Fixed code preserves the original parse result, using the control reader's own missing-file fallback. The pinned PM-linked run passed with result tracking disabled. The initial physical identity audit found one unrelated non-public address in the shared object database. A transport-cloned branch passed the same audit with five approved addresses. The registry I/O fixture now distinguishes four fresh receiver opens during proof collection and push from zero rereads on the two warm handles."
  "2026-11-26T18:05:03.767Z",codex-agent,"Round-three validation: Node 22 quick swept 104 referenced test files with 2,615 passes and five profile skips. The initial fault-injection and inventory failures passed their targeted reruns. The identity-dependent check is validated in a transport clone of the branch. The one-worker crash rerun passed 53/53. Node 26 self-host passed 108/108. Bun 1.3.14 self-host and tracker candidate passed 110/110. Built and npm-packed Node and Bun SDK plus project-installed CLI passed 6/6. The linked PM test, native TOON, installed-CLI strace, typecheck, build, test build, lint, duplication, docstrings, release verifiers and pack checks passed. Pack privacy found zero findings in 369 files and the production audit found zero vulnerabilities. Nine isolated behavioral reverts produced 13 expected failures. Exact-head CI will appear at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/pull/240/checks ."
  "2026-11-26T18:30:10.611Z",codex-agent,"CI run 45873477954 passed 21 jobs including all test shards and Linux/Windows release validation. Coverage merge measured 31582/31582 lines and statements, 1387/1387 functions, and 13724/13727 branches. Adding direct fault tests for the destruction intent post-read identity check, erasure audit nonregular descriptor check, and bounded object premature EOF check."
  "2026-11-26T18:35:03.953Z",codex-agent,"Coverage follow-up revert proof: each guard was removed separately in a disposable copy. The intent mutation, nonregular audit descriptor, and premature EOF cases each failed with Missing expected exception; the three fixed cases passed. The audit test asserts zero byte reads, the intent test preserves source files and new audit bytes, and the EOF test verifies descriptor cleanup and a successful retry. Typecheck, test build, lint, duplication, docstrings and changelog passed. The first CI coverage details are at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/45873477954/job/140101970690 . Exact-head checks for the amended branch are at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/pull/240/checks ."
  "2026-11-26T18:35:53.790Z",codex-agent,"Node 26 quick profile with two test workers passed 173/173 across test/destruction.test.ts, test/review-repair.test.ts and test/object-read-protocol.test.ts. The existing tracker file and architecture links cover these tests and their implementation paths. Rebuilt the tracker snapshot and verified changelog parity for the final commit."
  "2026-11-26T18:36:14.207Z",codex-agent,The linked command passed all three fault tests. Scoped c8 measurements hit each of the three exact guard branches missed in run 45873477954. CI remains responsible for merged package coverage and the release gates.
  "2026-11-26T19:07:00.915Z",codex-agent,Split requested after the combined branch passed exact-head CI. PR #240 now keeps the snapshot and script-facing helpers. Published engine descriptor changes and their proofs move to issue #241. The pre-split history is preserved. Earlier broad audit comments are historical evidence; the current file and test links describe the narrowed scope.
  "2026-11-26T19:13:07.042Z",codex-agent,"Non-script Git ledger, preflight and release-verifier changes are out of both scoped diffs and remain in the pre-split history. The plain Git command wrapper remains unchanged, so the strict script decoder no longer changes commit-log decoding. The snapshot reader continues to preserve valid control-byte paths and reject distinct invalid UTF-8 names."
  "2026-11-26T19:22:03.441Z",codex-agent,"Narrowed script branch validation: Node 26 self-host passed 108/108, Node 22 passed 108/108, and pinned Bun 1.3.14 passed 110/110 including the tracker candidate. The helper-reference sweep passed 471 assertions and exposed one shared Git object-store identity failure; the exact head is audited in a transport clone. The pinned PM linked regression passed. An isolated revert of strict decoding failed the two-name collision case with a missing expected refusal; restoring the guard passed 1/1. Typecheck, builds, lint, duplication, docs, and pack privacy passed. Exact-head CI will appear at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/pull/240/checks ."
  "2026-11-26T19:42:23.191Z",codex-agent,PRRT_kwDOToJT7M68iT-2 reproduced a staging deletion when the split script branch changed the shared engine reader without the native catch fix. Working-file capture is now private to scripts/self-host.ts and the engine tree matches main. Draft PR #242 already carries the staging catch guard at 04a2de9. Restoring only the old catch in a disposable copy made the exact non-Git replacement regression fail with a missing expected exception. Restoring the draft guard passed and preserved index bytes. Two isolated script reverts failed the new link test for lossy link rendering and skipping the post-read fence; restoring private capture passed.
  "2026-11-26T19:43:57.535Z",codex-agent,"Private script capture passed 152/152 Node 26 reader and helper-reference tests, 109/109 Node 22 reader tests, 111/111 Bun 1.3.14 reader and tracker-candidate tests, and the pinned PM raw-link regression. Typecheck, builds, lint, changelog preparation, duplication, docstrings, and pack privacy passed. The engine source diff against main is empty. Exact-head status is available at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/pull/240/checks ."
  "2026-11-26T20:47:00.898Z",codex-agent,"Review round at 9ad444f. Both complete threads contain one comment each and the latest CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff findings. The frozen tree is authoritative for source selection; the live index authorizes replacement of the existing bundle. Preserve the permission mode before publishing bytes, including read-only bundles. Production changes stay in scripts/self-host.ts."
  "2026-11-26T20:52:55.132Z",codex-agent,"Revert proofs for PRRT_kwDOToJT7M68jWmF and PRRT_kwDOToJT7M68jWmM. In isolated copies, frozen-tree tracking rejected the intent-to-add bundle, skipping the final index checks accepted a late index removal, using the process umask produced 0644 instead of 0600 at rename, and skipping the mode fence accepted a late chmod. Restoring a direct live-index probe raised the caller shared base mtime above its 1000 ms sentinel. The private-copy checks preserve both alternate split-index bytes and the referenced base timestamp for staged and working writes. All three regression cases passed with the fixed code restored."
  "2026-11-26T20:54:14.994Z",codex-agent,"Validation on the final script changes: the Node 26 targeted reader and referencing sweep passed 133/133, including the existing split-index sentinels; the focused cases passed 6/6, and the three regression cases passed 3/3 each on Node 22 and Bun 1.3.14. The linked pinned PM tests passed. Typecheck, builds, lint, duplication, docstrings and pack privacy passed. Changelog and the regenerated bundle are checked before push. Exact-head CI will appear at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/pull/240/checks ."
  "2026-11-26T21:43:09.367Z",codex-agent,"Review round at d574028 covers four inline findings: Windows pathspec casing, the replacement bundle group, lossless Git administrative paths, and split-index fallback by the selected symlink pathname. The latest review body also reports an index-only attributes discrepancy. In a real Git fixture, hash-object on captured CRLF bytes and git add produced different blob IDs with an index-only eol=lf rule. That separate advisory is outside this round’s explicit four-finding scope."
  "2026-11-26T21:51:26.452Z",codex-agent,"Four isolated revert proofs on the final implementation: PRRT_kwDOToJT7M68kS2B retained lowercase pathspec keys under Windows matching; PRRT_kwDOToJT7M68kS2E published instead of propagating EPERM, which the group-order and preservation regression caught; PRRT_kwDOToJT7M68kS2G substituted a byte and misleadingly reported missing self-host.json; PRRT_kwDOToJT7M68kS2J failed ENOENT beside the dereferenced index. Restoring the fixes passed 4/4, including the symlink-selected shared-base fixture with a parent symlink and dot components. Node 22, Node 26, Bun 1.3.14 and the pinned PM linked run passed all four cases."
  "2026-11-26T21:53:03.802Z",codex-agent,"Final pre-push scoped validation: Node 26 targeted and referencing suites passed 149/149; focused Node 22 and Bun 1.3.14 passed 4/4 each. Typecheck, builds, lint, duplication, docstrings, and pack privacy passed. Bun required the temporary descriptor UID explicitly rather than the negative chown sentinel, and the index reader uses descriptor I/O instead of lexically resolving symlink traversal. Separately reproduced that resolveRepoRoot returns a lossy spelling for a raw-byte worktree root. The index-only attributes and generic root-path findings are follow-up candidates under the explicit four-finding scope. Exact-head CI will appear at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/pull/240/checks ."
