body: "## Why this exists\n\nPull request 236 (\"Keep self-host bundles current in tracker automation\", squash commit 1504164) merged while the automated review of its last three commits (b6c7b3b, 1df3b53, bbabb7c: the object-database snapshot reader in `scripts/self-host.ts`) was still running. Those commits were reviewed after the merge. `accept:self-host` and `test/self-host.test.ts` (79 of 79) pass on main for this repository's own content; the findings below are inputs the reader mishandles.\n\n## Findings\n\nBlocking:\n\n1. **`scripts/self-host.ts:756`: lossy path decoding can hide a file from the gate.** Git paths ending in the raw bytes `0x80` and `0x81` both decode to the replacement character; the second entry overwrites the first, and the gate accepted a commit that changed the omitted file. Parse the listing as bytes and reject paths the bundle cannot represent losslessly.\n2. **`scripts/self-host.ts:845`: excluded large files exhaust the shared buffer.** Two excluded 33 MiB paths exceeded the 64 MiB buffer and failed both staged writing and verification. Read the configuration first, fetch only the required blobs, and stream their payloads.\n3. **`scripts/self-host.ts:807`: the batch parser accepts malformed answers.** Negative or blank sizes, a payload ending in `!` where a newline is required, and trailing output are accepted. Require exactly three header fields, an unsigned safe decimal size, a newline after each payload and exact exhaustion of the stream.\n4. **`scripts/self-host.ts:1050`: plain `--write` under `core.autocrlf=true` bundles CRLF files.** After committing the bundle, `--check` rejects it against the LF blobs. Generate the working-tree bundle from Git-cleaned bytes, or refuse converted inputs before writing and direct the caller to `--staged`.\n\nNon-blocking:\n\n5. **`scripts/self-host.ts:770`:** a `160000` entry is rejected even when the configuration explicitly excludes its path. Apply exclusions before rejecting unsupported modes.\n6. **`scripts/self-host.ts:1039`:** with a tracked edit staged, `git write-tree` rewrites the caller's index bytes (cache tree). Run against a temporary copy of the index and assert byte equality on the original.\n7. **`scripts/self-host.ts:886`:** plain `--write` follows a tracked `self-host.json` symlink, but the staged writer and the gate parse the link target text as JSON and fail. Enforce a regular configuration file consistently, or resolve tracked in-tree targets from the selected snapshot.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- One regression test per finding that fails on main and passes with the fix; the gate stays fail-closed for every reader error.\n- `accept:self-host` passes at the final commit with a regenerated bundle.\n- Works on Node 22, Node 26 and Bun as the existing suite does."
